gs that are registered in the City's RentSafeTO: Apartment Building Standards program.","license_id":"open-government-licence-toronto","license_title":"open-government-licence-toronto","is_open":true,"tags":[],"groups":[],"num_resources":4,"resource_formats":["CSV","JSON","XML"],"update_frequency":"Monthly","owner_unit":"Municipal Licensing & Standards","datastore_resources":1,"metadata_modified":"2026-07-05T09:00:25.639441","landing_page_url":"https://open.toronto.ca/dataset/apartment-building-registration/"}],"total_count":4,"returned_count":2,"start":0,"rows":2,"query":"apartment building evaluation","provenance":{"source":"ckan-toronto","url":"https://ckan0.cf.opendata.inter.prod-toronto.ca/api/3/action/package_search?q=apartment+building+evaluation&rows=2&start=0","queried_at":"2026-11-19T00:02:39.662262Z","as_of":null,"freshness":null,"coverage":"2 of 4 total matches returned","limits":"rows capped at 100 per request","cached":false,"lang":"en","schema_name":"ckan.PackageSearchResult","licence":"Licences differ by dataset on this platform: each dataset's own licence is in its licence fields. Check it before reusing.","commercial_use":"varies","caveats":[],"reproduce":"For scripts, call reproduce_code with this tool's name and arguments."}}},{"name":"ckan_get_dataset_documents","arguments":{"portal":"toronto","dataset_id":"apartment-building-evaluation","query":"score"},"response":{"portal":"toronto","dataset_id":"apartment-building-evaluation","title":"Apartment Building Evaluation","landing_page_url":"https://open.toronto.ca/dataset/apartment-building-evaluation/","description":"RentSafeTO: Apartment Building Standards is a bylaw enforcement program established in 2017 to ensure that owners and operators of apartment buildings with three or more storeys or 10 or more units comply with building maintenance standards. Learn more about [RentSafeTO](https://www.toronto.ca/community-people/housing-shelter/rental-housing-tenant-information/rental-housing-standards/apartment-building-standards/rentsafeto-for-tenants/).\r\n\r\nThis dataset contains building evaluation scores for buildings registered with RentSafeTO.  During evaluations, Bylaw Enforcement Officers inspect common areas, mechanical and security systems, parking and exterior grounds.\r\n\r\nIn 2023, RentsafeTO updated its evaluation process. Buildings must undergo evaluation at least once every two years, increasing the number of evaluation categories to 50 and allocating a weight to the category.\r\n\r\nEach category item is inspected and assigned a score from one to three with one being the lowest and three being the highest. At times, an item may be assigned a score of 0 if it cannot be evaluated due to an obstruction or refusal to inspect. Additionally, if an item is not applicable to the building at the time of evaluation, the score will show as blank in the dataset.\r\n\r\nTo download data from building evaluations before 2023, please download “Pre-2023 Apartment Building Evaluations\" and “Apartment Building Evaluations 2023 - current” to download data from building evaluations from 2023 and beyond.\r\n\r\nLearn more about [RentSafeTO: Evaluation Tool – City of Toronto](https://www.toronto.ca/community-people/housing-shelter/rental-housing-tenant-information/rental-housing-standards/apartment-building-standards/rentsafeto-evaluation-tool/).","about":{"dataset_category":"Table","is_retired":false,"information_url":"https://www.toronto.ca/community-people/housing-shelter/rental-housing-standards/apartment-building-standards/","topics":["City government","Locations and mapping","Business"],"refresh_rate":"Daily","owner_division":"Municipal Licensing & Standards","owner_section":"Policy & Strategic Support","last_refreshed":"2026-11-18 09:34:48.969032"},"data_dictionary":[{"resource_ids":["244f7a02-da5c-425b-b55f-fbdd133dd732"],"resource_names":["Apartment Building Evaluations 2023 - current"],"fields":[{"name":"YEAR EVALUATED","type":"int4","label":null,"description":"This represents the year of the building evaluation scores."},{"name":"CURRENT BUILDING EVAL SCORE","type":"text","label":null,"description":"An assessment of a building's compliance with property standards which is calculated by adding the reactive score (applicable Orders or Notices of Violations) to the proactive score (latest building evaluation score)"},{"name":"PROACTIVE BUILDING SCORE","type":"text","label":null,"description":"The score of the most recent, proactive evaluation of the common areas of a building reflecting the weighted score of all, applicable, evaluation categories."},{"name":"CURRENT REACTIVE SCORE","type":"text","label":null,"description":"Total score of all applicable Orders and Notices of Violation issued for a building"},{"name":"TENANT NOTIFICATION BOARD","type":"text","label":null,"description":"Display of planned or unplanned service disruptions, any pest control treatment activities, the apartment building's score, among other important notices for tenants. The Tenant Notification Board is a notification board (with notices posted commonly behind glass) in a central location within the apartment building."}],"fields_total":70},{"resource_ids":["b987be09-0c62-4d7d-928c-4a1ecaeaf3f3"],"resource_names":["Pre-2023 Apartment Building Evaluations"],"fields":[{"name":"SCORE","type":"text","label":null,"description":null},{"name":"RESULTS_OF_SCORE","type":"text","label":null,"description":null}],"fields_total":39}],"documents":[{"title":"Information page","url":"https://www.toronto.ca/community-people/housing-shelter/rental-housing-standards/apartment-building-standards/","kind":"information page","format":null},{"title":"RentSafeTO","url":"https://www.toronto.ca/community-people/housing-shelter/rental-housing-tenant-information/rental-housing-standards/apartment-building-standards/rentsafeto-for-tenants/","kind":"linked in the description","format":null},{"title":"RentSafeTO: Evaluation Tool – City of Toronto","url":"https://www.toro